  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-260000809</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Post FNS Scoping and Ideation Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Post scoping phase support the process of making the call for concept papers and selection process, the Embassy seeks to get additional backstopping support from the consultancy team, following a successful scoping and ideation phase. This will facilitate for post scoping and ideation support from the consultants once the call for concept paper is published. Since the call will be publicily published, a huge amount of interest and therefore application is anticipated. To better manage the anticipated huge amount of application that will be received, the Embassy seeks to extent the contract of the consultant team to offer necessary support that will ensure the selection process is efficient.
The scoping and ideation assignment was a short term consultancy task that aimed to inform new programming for food and nutrition security activities under the new MACS 2026-2029. This assignment carried out an analysis of the horticulture, livestock and fisheries value chains, applying the food systems framework, also integrating a water-energy-food nexus approach. The analysis will comprised  a comprehensive review of the Kenyan agrifood policy context, pinpointing policy and development priorities in relation to the shared interests with the Netherlands government&apos;s interest as outlined in the current foreign policy. The assignment also analysed the development partners&apos; landscape in the agrifood sector highlighting the key actors and trends, also inview of the Dutch diamond partner approach. The outcome of this comprehensive analysis are three program workstreams that will inform and guide the call for concept papers for new FNS programming.</narrative>
  </description>
